workedExamples.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.16cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,<->] (-2,0)--(52,0);
\foreach \v in {0,...,50} {\draw[black] (\v,-0.05)--(\v,0.05);}
\foreach \v in {0,10,...,50} {\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,-0.12) {$\v$};}
\node[below] at (25,-0.65) {Score};
\draw[black,thick] (8,1.3)--(14,1.3) (37,1.3)--(49,1.3);
\draw[black,thick] (8,1.1)--(8,1.5) (49,1.1)--(49,1.5);
\draw[black,thick] (14,0.9) rectangle (37,1.7);
\draw[black,thick] (18,0.9)--(18,1.7);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) State the values at the two ends of the box.
(b) Find the length of the right whisker.
(c) Is the median line allowed to be this close to the left edge of the box?

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) The box runs from $Q_1=14$ to $Q_3=37$.
(b) The right whisker runs from $37$ to the maximum $49$.
Length:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}49-37\\&=12\end{aligned}$
(c) Yes. The median is $18$, the middle value of the ordered data. It need not be halfway between $14$ and $37$. The quartile sections can have different widths.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.16cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,<->] (-2,0)--(52,0);
\foreach \v in {0,...,50} {\draw[black] (\v,-0.05)--(\v,0.05);}
\foreach \v in {0,10,...,50} {\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,-0.12) {$\v$};}
\node[below] at (25,-0.65) {Score};
\draw[black,thick] (8,1.3)--(14,1.3) (37,1.3)--(49,1.3);
\draw[black,thick] (8,1.1)--(8,1.5) (49,1.1)--(49,1.5);
\draw[black,thick] (14,0.9) rectangle (37,1.7);
\draw[black,thick] (18,0.9)--(18,1.7);
\foreach \v in {14,18,37,49} {\draw[black,dashed,thin] (\v,0)--(\v,0.85);}
\node[above] at (14,2.35) {$Q_1=14$};
\node[above] at (18,1.85) {Median $18$};
\node[above] at (37,1.85) {$Q_3=37$};
\node[above] at (49,2.35) {Maximum $49$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

